# Git mailmap — remaps author/committer identities for `git log`,
# `git blame`, `git shortlog`, and GitHub's web UI without rewriting
# history.
#
# Format (see `git help mailmap`):
#   <correct-email>                       <bad-email>
#   Correct Name <correct-email>          Bad Name <bad-email>
#
# Add a new entry below whenever a contributor's git identity was
# misconfigured. Never delete entries — they must keep mapping
# historical commits forever.

# 2026-08-04 — initial import + v1.0.0-beta.1 release commits were
# authored with a typo email (missing `l` in `gmail`, extra `m` in
# `com`). Config fixed globally at the same date.
Bonti Haryanto <bonti.haryanto@gmail.com> <bonti.haryanto@gmai.comm>
